CC   IMGT/LIGM-DB annotation level: by annotators
CC   
CC   For an overview of the D-J-C region entries see the first paragraph
CC   of the comment in segment 1.
CC       Diversity segments code for the third hypervariable or
CC   complementarity determining region of the variable region.  They
CC   are divided into 3 families by sequence homology, D-FL16, D-SP2 and
CC   D-Q.  It is believed that there are 12 D segments, although there
CC   may be some segments 5' to D-FL16.1 which have not been discovered.
CC   Known sequences of rearranged D segments suggest that greater
CC   variability may be generated by D-D recombination.  The putative
CC   recombination recognition sequences noted in the Sites table
CC   consist of a nonamer-12bp spacer-palindromic heptamer 5' to the D
CC   sequence and a palindromic heptamer-12bp spacer-nonamer 3' to the D
CC   sequence.
CC       [9] sequenced a rearranged gene, but since the area reported is
CC   3' to the rearrangements, it is presumed to correspond to the
CC   germline sequence.  However, the conflicts in the sites table
CC   involving [9] may be due to the known high rate of somatic mutation
CC   in recombined variable regions.
CC       The J-H sequences encode the C-terminus of the third
CC   hypervariable region and the C-terminus of the variable region. The
CC   putative recombination recognition sequences 5' to the coding
CC   sequences are found before all J sequences, light- and heavy-chain.
CC   [9] identifies a putative pseudo-J-H sequence within bases
CC   2016-2088, which contains termination codons in all reading frames.
CC       The experimentally verified enhancer region noted in the Sites
CC   table has only been localized to within the PstI-EcoRI fragment
CC   (bases 3247-3559) [12],[13].
CC       Only the germline S-mu region is reported with these entries.
CC   For rearranged S-mu regions see the rearranged heavy chain entries.
CC       The clone used by [3] contains a 2.8kb deletion which is a
CC   cloning artifact.  [8] has identified the extent of this deletion
CC   (from base 5427 in this entry to base 773 in <MUSIGCD09>), but
CC   there is some uncertainty (+-5bp) due to the highly repetitive
CC   nature of the S-mu region.  The S-mu region covers over 3kb and is
CC   primarily made up of two repeating pentamers (gagct)n (ggggt),
CC   which are believed to act as recognition sequences for S-S
CC   recombination.
CC      Figures 2 and 4 of [3] report different bases for bases 2373 and
CC   2392.  We have used the bases from figure 4 because they agree with
CC   those in [9].
CC      For rearranged D and J segments see the rearranged heavy chain
CC   entries.  Data from [13] kindly reviewed (23-AUG-1983) by W.
CC   Schaffner.
CC   Complete source information:
CC   Mouse BALB/c liver DNA [4],[14]; embryo DNA [3],[7]; BALB/c newborn
CC   DNA [2],[10],[8]; BALB/c sperm DNA [1],[5],[6]; myeloma HPC76 DNA
CC   [9],[13]; BALB/c hybridoma 24.13 DNA [11]; myeloma MOPC 141 DNA
CC   [12].
